---
import Curve from "../components/Curve.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import "../css/reset.css";
import "../css/global.css";
import "../css/index.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Learn more about Kevin and Starburst Digital."
    />
    <title>About - Starburst Digital</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="flow section spot-color-primary">
      <h2 class="wrapper mt-m-l">Starburst Digital</h2>
      <nav class="" style="padding-top:1px;padding-bottom:1px;">
        <ul class="cluster wrapper" role="list">
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <div class="section spot-color-primary">
        <div class="section__inner">
          <div class="wrapper flow region">
            <h1>About Me</h1>
          </div>
        </div>
        <Curve />
      </div>
      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <div class="grid" data-layout="50-50">
          <div>
            <img
              src="https://placehold.co/600x800"
              alt="Kevin, founder of Starburst Digital"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="flow">
            <p>
              I'm Kevin, a software engineer who's been building web
              applications for over a decade. I've worked on everything from
              mission-critical systems for first responders to real estate
              platforms and marketing tools.
            </p>
            <p>
              After years of working with enterprise clients, I realized that
              small businesses were getting a raw deal. Most developers either
              charge enterprise prices or use cookie-cutter templates that don't
              actually solve problems.
            </p>
            <p>
              That's why I started Starburst Digital. I wanted to bring the same
              level of craftsmanship I apply to enterprise work to small
              businesses who need it most—without the enterprise price tag.
            </p>
            <p>
              When you work with me, you're getting a real engineer who
              understands performance, accessibility, and modern web standards.
              Not someone slapping together a WordPress theme or deploying
              generic templates.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="section spot-color-secondary">
        <Curve />
        <div class="section__inner">
          <article class="flow region wrapper">
            <h2>What I Believe</h2>
            <p>
              The web should be fast, accessible, and owned by the people who
              create content for it. You shouldn't need to be locked into a
              platform or pay exorbitant fees just to have a professional online
              presence.
            </p>
            <p>
              Good software is thoughtful software. It's built with real
              understanding of how people use it, not just copy-pasted from
              tutorials or generated by AI without human oversight.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <Curve />
      </div>

      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>Let's Work Together</h2>
        <p>
          If you're a small business owner who wants a real website built by a
          real developer, I'd love to hear from you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
